course: dictionary
lesson: 9222
title: Somebody: a person we do not name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Somebody is a pronoun. It stands in for a person when we do not know who they are, or when we do not say who they are. «Somebody left a bag by the door.» We do not know the name of the person, so the writer says somebody.
explain: Somebody means the same as someone. Both can be used in the same way: «Somebody has taken my pencil» and «Someone has taken my pencil» mean exactly the same thing.
explain: Read the verb to see what somebody has to do. «The boat cannot cross empty, so somebody must row it back.» The verb row tells you the job. In maths, a sentence like «Somebody took 5 sweets» tells you to take away.
explain: A somebody, with the word a in front, is a noun. It means an important or famous person. «He wants to be a somebody» means he wants to become someone important.
fact: Somebody is a pronoun that means a person whose name is not known or not said.
fact: Somebody means the same as someone.
fact: You can add else or special to make phrases: somebody else, somebody special.
fact: «A somebody» is a noun that means an important or famous person.
fact: If somebody you do not know offers you a lift, say no and tell an adult you trust.
exercise: «Somebody left a lunchbox on the bus.» What does somebody mean here? | *A person whose name is not known or not said | A famous actor on the bus | A cupboard for lunches | A lunch that has already been eaten
exercise: Which word means the same as somebody? | Anybody | Nobody | *Someone | Everybody
exercise: Mia says, «He wants to be a somebody.» What does a somebody mean? | A small insect | A nobody with no friends | A person who sings in the choir | *An important or famous person
test: «The boat cannot cross empty, so somebody must row it back.» What must somebody do in this sentence? | Sink the boat | Stay on the other bank | *Row the boat back | Sleep in the boat
test: Sam had 12 sweets and somebody took 5 away. How many sweets are left? | 12 | *7 | 5 | 17
exam: If somebody you do not know offers you a lift, what should you do? | Give them your home address | Get in quickly before they drive away | *Say no and tell an adult you trust | Wait and see what happens
